<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">François de Laval</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1623">1623</a>–<a href="/years/1708">1708</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">François de Laval was the first Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a>, arriving in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a> in 1659 as vicar apostolic and becoming bishop when the diocese was created in 1674. He founded the Seminary of Quebec in 1663, organised parishes and clashed with governors over the sale of brandy to indigenous peoples. Canonised in 2014, he gives his name to Université Laval.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francois-de-laval.jpg" alt="François de Laval" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fran%C3%A7ois_de_Laval_-_Project_Gutenberg_eText_17174.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
